{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ViewSpacing\/distance(to:along:)"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ViewSpacing"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/viewspacing\/distance(to:along:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"distance"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"next"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ViewSpacing","text":"ViewSpacing","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI11ViewSpacingV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"along"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"axis"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Axis","text":"Axis","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4AxisO"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sf","text":"Float"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The spacing preferences instance of the adjacent view."}]}],"name":"next"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The axis that the two views align on.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"axis"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A floating point value that represents the smallest distance","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in points between two views that satisfies the spacing preferences","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of both this view and the adjacent views on their shared edge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call this method from your implementation of "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Layout","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"methods if you need to measure the default spacing between two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"views in a custom layout. Call the method on the first view’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"preferences instance, and provide the second view’s preferences"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance as input."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, consider two views that appear in a custom horizontal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stack. The following distance call gets the preferred spacing between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"these views, where "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spacing1"},{"type":"text","text":" contains the preferences of a first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"view, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spacing2"},{"type":"text","text":" contains the preferences of a second view:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["let distance = spacing1.distance(to: spacing2, axis: .horizontal)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The method first determines, based on the axis and the ordering, that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the views abut on the trailing edge of the first view and the leading","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge of the second. It then gets the spacing preferences for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corresponding edges of each view, and returns the greater of the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values. This results in the smallest value that provides enough space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to satisfy the preferences of both views.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This method returns the default spacing between views, but a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"layout can choose to ignore the value and use custom spacing instead."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gets the preferred spacing distance along the specified axis to the view"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that returns a specified spacing preference."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI11ViewSpacingV8distance2to5alongSfAC_AA4AxisOtF","title":"distance(to:along:)","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"distance"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI11ViewSpacingV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ViewSpacing"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"along"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4AxisO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Axis"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sf","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Float"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Layout":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Layout","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Layout","type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/